WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.208


2
00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:31.583
<b>Sri Krishna</b>

3
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:36.125
<b>was discussing the senses and the</b>
<b>experiences they generate.</b>

4
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:44.166
<b>He emphasized developing patience towards</b>
<b>temporary experiences in this fleeting world.</b>

5
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:44.875
<b>Now,</b>

6
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:47.208
<b>He tells Arjuna</b>

7
00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:50.708
<b>that one who remains unaffected</b>
<b>by such experiences,</b>

8
00:00:50.708 --> 00:00:55.625
<b>who views both joy and sorrow</b>
<b>with the same perspective,</b>

9
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:56.958
<b>that wise</b>

10
00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:59.375
<b>one can attain</b>

11
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.166
<b>immortality.</b>

12
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:06.083


13
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:12.250
<b>Favourable or unfavourable, when you</b>
<b>cultivate patience towards all circumstances,</b>

14
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.666
<b>and consistently perform your duty,</b>

15
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:18.875
<b> this develops wisdom within you.</b>

16
00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:23.375
<b>And it is this wisdom that will</b>
<b>lead you towards liberation.</b>

17
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:28.291
<b>It’s important for us to</b>
<b>maintain stability in both states.</b>

18
00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:31.958
<b>Neither should we sink deeply into</b>
<b>the tides of sorrow,</b>

19
00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:37.708
<b>nor should we let success make</b>
<b>us feel larger than life.</b>

20
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:41.416
<b>For joy and sorrow are like seasons</b>

21
00:01:41.416 --> 00:01:42.583
<b>they come</b>

22
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:43.333
<b>and</b>

23
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:44.916
<b>go.</b>

24
00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:46.041
<b>But</b>

25
00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:49.000
<b>a question might arise in your mind:</b>

26
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.500
<b>If every problem, </b>

27
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.416
<b>every sorrow</b>

28
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:53.083
<b>is like a season</b>

29
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.416
<b>that will pass,</b>

30
00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:58.625
<b>should we just wait patiently for it to go away?</b>

31
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:01.625
<b>Is action unnecessary?</b>

32
00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:02.416
<b>No,</b>

33
00:02:02.416 --> 00:02:03.625
<b>that's not the case.</b>

34
00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:04.541
<b>It's essential</b>

35
00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:12.375
<b>that we take whatever action is needed to</b>
<b>resolve that sorrow or trouble.</b>

36
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:14.291
<b>And this is where we need to understand</b>

37
00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:18.666
<b>the meaning of that patience,</b>
<b>that composure.</b>

38
00:02:18.666 --> 00:02:20.750
<b>We must take necessary actions,</b>

39
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.666
<b>but without attaching our heart to</b>
<b>the outcomes of that action,</b>

40
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:29.791
<b>neither becoming excessively distressed</b>
<b>nor overly elated.</b>

41
00:02:29.791 --> 00:02:32.291
<b>This is the mark of excellence</b>

42
00:02:32.291 --> 00:02:34.750
<b>when we're not disheartened by adversity,</b>

43
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.083
<b>but simply act to improve the situation.</b>

44
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:42.541
<b>Similarly, we don't get carried</b>
<b>away in good times,</b>

45
00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:45.125
<b>knowing that what's here today</b>

46
00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:47.500
<b>may not be tomorrow.</b>

47
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.333
<b>When we adopt this kind of equanimity</b>

48
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:52.500
<b>and keep performing our duties,</b>

49
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.791
<b>it leads us towards supreme happiness,</b>

50
00:02:55.791 --> 00:02:58.875
<b>towards liberation.</b>

51
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:03.750


52
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.375
<b>Liberation.</b>

53
00:03:06.375 --> 00:03:10.416
<b>What does liberation mean?</b>

54
00:03:10.416 --> 00:03:18.666
<b>Does it only refer to the freedom</b>
<b>attained after death?</b>

55
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:21.875
<b>Listen to this word once again,</b>

56
00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:24.291
<b>and understand.</b>

57
00:03:24.291 --> 00:03:26.833
<b>Liberation.</b>

58
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:33.708
<b>Why should we wait for</b>
<b>death to attain liberation?</b>

59
00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:39.833
<b>We can attain liberation in the present,</b>
<b>in this very life.</b>

60
00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:42.291
<b>Liberation from joy and sorrow,</b>

61
00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:44.416
<b>liberation from ego,</b>

62
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:47.583
<b>liberation from the shackles that trouble us.</b>

63
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:53.000
<b>Isn't this liberation too?</b>

64
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.791
<b>Try to understand with this example</b>

65
00:03:57.791 --> 00:04:01.000
<b>Someone said something hurtful to you,</b>

66
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.625
<b>you got angry,</b>

67
00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:10.291
<b>you gave a harsh reply,</b>
<b>and before you knew it, the argument escalated.</b>

68
00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:14.333
<b>Are you truly free in such a situation?</b>

69
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:17.541
<b>Because you didn't want trouble,</b>

70
00:04:17.541 --> 00:04:20.208
<b>yet you got troubled.</b>

71
00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:23.833
<b>You didn't want to get angry, yet you did.</b>

72
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:28.833
<b>Words you didn't mean to say came out.</b>

73
00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:32.333
<b>When you lost control over yourself,</b>

74
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:34.583
<b>how do call yourself independent?</b>

75
00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:37.958
<b>How can you be free?</b>

76
00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:40.458
<b>Now, if you decide</b>

77
00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:46.375
<b>that someone's harsh words</b>
<b>don't make you a bad person,</b>

78
00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:55.416
<b>if you just listen to them with a smile and</b>
<b>bear it without giving the reaction they want</b>

79
00:04:55.416 --> 00:04:56.625
<b>isn't</b>

80
00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:59.375
<b>that a kind of freedom,</b>

81
00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:02.333
<b>a kind of liberation?</b>

82
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:05.750
<b>Because here, you're not a slave</b>
<b>to someone's words,</b>

83
00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.291
<b>you're not a slave to your anger,</b>

84
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:10.875
<b>your every action is independent.</b>

85
00:05:10.875 --> 00:05:12.958
<b>It's free.</b>

86
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:19.375
<b>This is the meaning of liberation</b>
<b>attained through patience.</b>

87
00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:24.166


88
00:05:24.166 --> 00:05:26.041
<b>In relationships,</b>

89
00:05:26.041 --> 00:05:28.625
<b>it often happens</b>

90
00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:30.875
<b>that in anger</b>

91
00:05:30.875 --> 00:05:33.083
<b>or irritation,</b>

92
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:40.458
<b>we say things to family members</b>
<b>that hurt them.</b>

93
00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:44.708
<b>Sometimes it's due to a disagreement,</b>

94
00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:50.250
<b>other times the reason for</b>
<b>irritation is completely different,</b>

95
00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.041
<b>but the arrows of words end up</b>
<b>hitting our loved ones.</b>

96
00:05:54.041 --> 00:05:58.666
<b>And once these word-arrows leave our mouths,</b>

97
00:05:58.666 --> 00:06:00.708
<b>they don't return,</b>

98
00:06:00.708 --> 00:06:06.666
<b>needlessly wounding the</b>
<b>hearts of our dear ones.</b>

99
00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:12.125
<b>Sometimes these wounds never heal.</b>

100
00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:18.416
<b>How essential patience</b>
<b>becomes for our relationships.</b>

101
00:06:18.416 --> 00:06:21.875
<b>It's natural, isn't it,</b>

102
00:06:21.875 --> 00:06:25.666
<b>that someone else's perspective</b>
<b>will be different from ours,</b>

103
00:06:25.666 --> 00:06:29.250
<b>their likes and dislikes might be opposite,</b>

104
00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:34.000
<b>their way of doing things might be different.</b>

105
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.041
<b>In such situations, considering them</b>
<b>wrong and ourselves right,</b>

106
00:06:38.041 --> 00:06:39.708
<b>and not just that,</b>

107
00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:43.416
<b>but losing our tolerance</b>

108
00:06:43.416 --> 00:06:46.708
<b>how can this be right?</b>

109
00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:50.875
<b>When we remain patient with our loved ones,</b>

110
00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:55.958
<b>when we scatter fragrant flowers from</b>
<b>our mouths instead of bitter arrows,</b>

111
00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:59.666
<b>a sweet nectar dissolves into relationships,</b>

112
00:06:59.666 --> 00:07:05.666
<b>which can even act as a</b>
<b>balm to heal old wounds.</b>

113
00:07:05.666 --> 00:07:07.208
<b>Stay patient,</b>

114
00:07:07.208 --> 00:07:08.416
<b>stay gentle,</b>

115
00:07:08.416 --> 00:07:10.250
<b>stay sweet.</b>

116
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:14.333


117
00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:16.125
<b>Any great work</b>

118
00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:18.083
<b>is not accomplished by scattered efforts,</b>

119
00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:18.833
<b>but</b>

120
00:07:18.833 --> 00:07:23.166
<b>by continuous dedication.</b>

121
00:07:23.166 --> 00:07:24.250
<b>And for this reason,</b>

122
00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:28.625
<b>in the professional world, those</b>
<b>who are at the pinnacle of success,</b>

123
00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:31.458
<b>have one quality in common,</b>

124
00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:32.583
<b>and that is</b>

125
00:07:32.583 --> 00:07:34.000
<b>Stability.</b>

126
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.375
<b>Remaining steady day after day,</b>

127
00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:43.083
<b>not deviating from your</b>
<b>goal in good times or bad.</b>

128
00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:44.500
<b>But what if</b>

129
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:49.250
<b>we get immediately discouraged</b>
<b>by adverse results?</b>

130
00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.458
<b>Will this discouragement help us?</b>

131
00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:57.291
<b>Will the results turn in our favour because</b>
<b>of this discouragement?</b>

132
00:07:57.291 --> 00:07:58.625
<b>No, right?</b>

133
00:07:58.625 --> 00:08:04.041
<b>So then, what will make</b>
<b>the results favourable to you?</b>

134
00:08:04.041 --> 00:08:08.958
<b>That will happen when you</b>
<b>compose yourself in bad times</b>

135
00:08:08.958 --> 00:08:13.833
<b>and focus on the next step of your duty.</b>

136
00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:16.708
<b>Understand this with an example</b>

137
00:08:16.708 --> 00:08:19.458
<b>If someone is taking exams,</b>

138
00:08:19.458 --> 00:08:23.625
<b>and in one subject,</b>
<b>the question paper was difficult,</b>

139
00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:25.250
<b>the exam went badly.</b>

140
00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:28.916
<b>So what would be better for success?</b>

141
00:08:28.916 --> 00:08:34.416
<b>To become distressed about this one subject</b>
<b>and lose focus on the upcoming subjects?</b>

142
00:08:34.416 --> 00:08:35.125
<b>Or</b>

143
00:08:35.125 --> 00:08:39.750
<b>to continuously strive for</b>
<b>the remaining subjects?</b>

144
00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.125
<b>You tell me?</b>

145
00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:43.791
<b>Continuous effort,</b>

146
00:08:43.791 --> 00:08:45.000
<b>Stability,</b>

147
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.791
<b>is a very important lesson in professional life.</b>

